        "explanationEn": "The correct opening line of Shloka 165 is «अन्याऽवगुणदोषादिवार्तां कदाऽपि नोच्चरेत्।».\nMeaning: One should never speak of another’s drawbacks or flaws. Doing so causes unrest and results in the displeasure of Bhagwan and the guru. (165)",
        "fullSanskritDevanagari": "अन्याऽवगुणदोषादिवार्तां कदाऽपि नोच्चरेत्।\nतथाकृते त्वशान्तिः स्याद् अप्रीतिश्च हरेर्गुरोः॥ १६५॥",
