        "explanationEn": "This divine teaching is expressed in Shloka 216: «सङ्गोऽत्र बलवाँल्लोके यथासङ्गं हि जीवनम्। सतां सङ्गम् अतः कुर्यात् कुसङ्गं सर्वथा त्यजेत्॥»\nMeaning: In this world, the company one keeps has great influence. The type of association molds one’s life accordingly. Therefore, one should always keep the company of virtuous people and totally shun bad company. (216)",
